    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Change\n\nThe task was to return `membershipTier: 'SILVER'` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `'BRONZE'`.\n\nSince `membershipTier` is a **derived** value computable entirely from fields already on the `Owner` (its `namesakeCount`, assigned on create, and its `email`), I exposed it as a read-only response field computed in the mapper \u2014 no new persistence or controller logic needed.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` response schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time), documented alongside the existing derived fields like `membershipNumber`.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that populates it via a new `membershipTier(owner)` helper:\n\n```java\ndefault String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n    boolean uniqueName = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;\n    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n    return uniqueName && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the existing convention used for `displayName` and `initials` (mapper-computed derived fields).\n\n## Tests\n- `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`): **pass**\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`",
